// ============================================================================
//  imgLogMeetingBtn.Visible  -  who can see the "Log a meeting" button.
// ============================================================================
// Only NON S-CODED people can see (and therefore use) the meeting logger.
// Reads the signed-in user's row straight off the model, so it needs
// 'S Coded?' in the Power BI visual's field well.
//
// The second line is a TESTING addition so the programme owner can see
// the button even though their record is not Non S-Coded. It uses the
// REAL signed-in email, because varUserEmail is remapped for some
// accounts in the dashboard build. Delete that line for production.
LookUp(
    PowerBIIntegration.Data,
    Trim( Lower( 'User Email' & "" ) ) = Trim( Lower( varUserEmail ) )
).'S Coded?' = "Non S-Coded (Phil)"
|| Lower( User().Email ) = "alex.cohen@hpe.com"
